      "writtenOn": "2018-09-14T07:35:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you add some negative test cases as well that show that you correctly can\u0027t find a socket that doesn\u0027t exist, without any exceptions?\n\nOne way to do this is to create a socket without SO_REUSEPORT, connect it, find the source port, close it, and then check to see if you can find the socket. The lack of SO_REUSEPORT should ensure that no other socket can use the same local IP address and port, and thus I think you are guaranteed that the socket does not exist.",
